# C2 panic-stack call chain, symbolized from disk (4.4.4) — evidence

# Purpose: §45 pinned the trap (quickjs.c:1494, `js_rc`'s `container_of`) and §46 pinned the last
# allocator event before it (`Mx size=ff0`), but the eight in-DLL frames both logs recorded were never
# turned into a named chain: §45's own boundary says "the middle of the chain is inferred". This log does
# that one thing — it symbolizes the eight RVAs that are ALREADY ON DISK in `c2_selfabort_4_4_4.log` and
# `c2_mfrecords_4_4_4.log` with the maintained offline tool, and writes the chain down with the source
# lines that name each frame. Nothing is measured on a running process.
# Second purpose: install the misreading guard that this job exposed. `func` was fed a bare RVA and
# answered "not inside any .pdata function entry" + exit 1 — the same sentence and the same code as the
# real finding. That is now exit 2, see (8).
