## (2) frame ORDER comes from the stderr dump, not from the sorted RVA line

The order is the child's panic print, verbatim at `evidence/logs/c2_selfabort_4_4_4.log:36-45` (frame 1 is
innermost, i.e. the trap itself):

    [repro] child stderr = "thread 7632 panic: member access within null pointer of type 'JSMallocBlockHeader' (aka 'struct JSMallocBlockHeader')
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc138cbd9b in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc139aede3 in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc138debde in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc138c55f5 in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc138c43bc in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc13bdb9c8 in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc13bdcc05 in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      ???:?:?: 0x7ffc13d0d339 in ??? (sqjs_s43.dll)
      … then libffi-8.dll, _ctypes.pyd, python313.dll, python.exe, KERNEL32.DLL, ntdll.dll frames"

Subtracting that run's own `BASE sqjs_s43.dll 0x7ffc138c0000` (`:35`) turns each line into an RVA:
`0xbd9b, 0xeede3, 0x1ebde, 0x55f5, 0x43bc, 0x31b9c8, 0x31cc05, 0x44d339`. **The sorted line `:48` —
`0x43bc, 0x55f5, 0xbd9b, 0x1ebde, 0xeede3, 0x31b9c8, 0x31cc05, 0x44d339` — is a set, not an order**, and so
are §46's sorted dumps — `c2_mfrecords_4_4_4.log:107` and `:127` (this artifact's set) plus the comparison
pair `:172`/`:173` (which prints §45's set alongside).
Reading the sorted line as a stack would put `JS_NewRuntime2` innermost of everything, i.e. upside down.

For the §46 bytes only the innermost frame is printed as a stack line (`c2_mfrecords_4_4_4.log:103`:
`???:?:?: 0x7ffc125bbd9b in ??? (sqjs_s46.dll)`, then `:104` "… 7 further in-DLL frames"). The order is
carried across by identity: 7 of the 8 RVAs are literally the same numbers in §45 and §46, and §46 says so
at `:176` ("Five of eight frames are the same RVA; only the outermost moved" — five *resolved* the same,
eight *numbers* are shared except one). So position 1..7 is taken from §45's stderr and position 8 is
§46's moved `0x44e399`. This is recorded as an inference from a stated identity, not as a fresh ordering
observation.

